  "question": {
    "text": "A transformer is used to light a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>110</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> lamp from a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> mains. If the current is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, the efficiency of the transformer is<!-- MathType@End@5@5@ -->"
